A||||3||David DeVoe||exhaust heat shields||||5||
Z||000000||David DeVoe||12-30-2001||11:00 AM||||I'm curious as to what kind of finish (if any) the heat shields had on them. I'm thinking of refinishing some with hi temp paint but from all I've read here on the forum the Fiero exhaust runs mighty hot and most finishes don't last. Has anyone done something like this??<BR>Dave||||reg||5
Z||000001||avengador1||12-30-2001||11:37 AM||||You could use high temp coatings from <A HREF="http://www.eastwoodcompany.com" TARGET=_blank>www.eastwoodcompany.com</A>  Im using the silver coating on my exhaust and heat shields with good results. The coating is actually heat cured. Hope this helps. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||12-30-2001||03:59 PM||||<A HREF="http://www.techlinecoatings.com/" TARGET=_blank>Tech Line Coatings</A> sells DIY coatings for various parts.... for a heat sheild you'll probably have to bake the part to get uniform curing... <P>You'll also want a heat reflective coating vs an insulating coating that you'd put on the exhaust itself.||||reg||1
Z||000003||88CoupeV6||12-30-2001||06:32 PM||||I just want to vent on how I hate the 88 heat shild on the crossover pipe!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> I think I am going to use the one from my 86 GT. The 88 one rattles and is like foil.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P><BR>Sorry.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||8
